From 5386a0fc357564c0767ecfa06c9a1c55bc9010ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:31:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] power: supply: apple: classify chargers across role
 changes and replug

Serialize analog Apple/BC1.2 sampling with the S8000 role hardware mutex
and discard samples interrupted by gadget events. Preserve source identity
across USB link PM, and advance a physical source epoch on observed VBUS
removal so a fast replug cannot preserve the prior charger override.
Forget gadget grants and camera-adapter handshake state on that removal.

Use the board ceiling for an ordinary USB host on every attach, with
source ceilings retained for bricks, BC1.2 and ACA. Keep explicit current
writes as per-attach caps. Preserve the existing battery guards and gadget
configuration path.

Back off on an observed lower PMU input setting instead of immediately
fighting it. Hold for 60 seconds and retry one bounded step per minute.
Expose source ceiling, live setting and cause in charge7_state. This does
not claim voltage-based droop protection: the iOS D2365 backend supplies
neither input-limited indication nor measured input current, and no safe
VBUS ADC or VINDPM configuration has been verified.

Tested with actual-code userspace harnesses, ASan/UBSan, concurrent role
locking, existing accessory/ID-bus regressions, and fresh W=1 objects.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
